+## The combat detail option in levels (LV9, 2026-11-15; plan 8.7 and 7.2)
+
+`core/src/levels_detail.c`, `core/include/doomo/lv_detail.h`. What a level gives up in each mode of
+Options > Performance > Combat detail (`OPT_3D_FAST`: Balanced, Smooth, Max detail), and how many awake
+demons it may have. Pure functions on a caller-owned 4-byte `LvDetail`: no statics, no clock, no rng.
+
+* **Header keys.** `detail a,b,c` (up to 3 of `floors sky props fx far light steam rain crowd decals loot`,
+  first dropped first; the five new kinds are append-only in `MDET_*`) and `awake S B M` (new, stored in
+  `DoomoMapExt.awake[3]`, 0 0 0 = not given). mapc checks `1..48`, not falling, and on a `gba yes` map at most
+  6 8 10 (plan 7.2). A map without the key emits `{0, 0, 0}`; the 12 shipped maps are v1 and unchanged.
+* **Dropped effects.** Steps = (Smooth ? 2 : 0) + the held pressure level (0..3), at most the list's length;
+  step n drops the n-th named effect. So Balanced and Max drop nothing in budget and lose the list one effect
+  at a time under pressure; Smooth starts with two gone. `lvd_get` returns the mask (`1 << MDET_*`).
+* **Pressure and hysteresis.** `lvd_pressure(cost_pct)` turns a frame's cost in percent of its budget into
+  0..3 (<= 100, <= 115, <= 140, above). `lvd_update` goes one step down per update while the pressure is
+  above the held level and one step back only after 45 good updates (1.5 s at 30 fps); an alternating
+  over / under signal holds the level; a change of mode restarts the state. Nobody feeds pressure yet (the
+  GBA / PS1 / DC governors are platform code that does not talk to the core): the hook below runs with
+  pressure 0 until a platform does.
+* **Awake cap.** `awake S B M` x the platform (GBA 1, PS1 1.5, Dreamcast 2); defaults 6 / 8 / 10 (the Vape
+  Cellar numbers of plan 7.2). The governor lowers Balanced and Max one demon per level toward Smooth's cap
+  and no lower. The cap is not enforced by the spawner yet: there is no level with a v2 header to enforce
+  it on, and the AI hot path stays untouched (LV6 owns the awake logic).
+* **Loot and props under Smooth.** `detail ... loot` (small health, ammo, candy) and `... props` thin the
+  spawns: every second one by thing index, in Smooth only, whatever the pressure (a level plays the same
+  at any frame cost). `lvd_thing_kept` never drops a key, armor, big health, scrap, a soul orb, an NPC or a
+  demon, a `secret` / boss / dormant / kill-event / machine-heart thing, or one flagged `collect`, `escort` or
+  `usable` (test: every thing type x every flag x several indices).
+* **Hooks (behind the same option).** `combat.c` (spawn loop: `lvd_thing_kept`) and `combat_scene.c`
+  (`combat_view_detail`: a level whose list names `fx` also drops the non-player shadows), both through
+  `map_ext_of(doomo_map.def)`, which is NULL for every v1 map today (an empty registry walk). Compiled out on
+  the PS1 (`#if !defined(DOOMO_PLATFORM_PS1)`: no resident byte, no overlay growth). The renderers' own
+  steam, rain, crowd and decal billboards do not exist yet; a level that adds them reads
+  `LvDetailOut.drop` the same way. Persistent state (`LvDetail`, 4 B) is not stored anywhere yet: it needs a
+  home when a platform feeds pressure (the `LvRun` has no spare bytes: net-zero EWRAM rules out +4).
+* **Tests.** `core/tests/test_lv_detail.c` (every mode x every held level, hysteresis, platforms, defaults,
+  stale state, the never-drop rules, determinism) on `core/tests/maps/t9_detail.txt`; `tools/tests/test_mapc.py`
+  (the `awake` key, the new kinds, the GBA limit).
+
